BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Maurer School of Law
DTSTART:20261019T160000Z
DTEND:20261019T170000Z
LOCATION:LOWELL E. BAIER HALL/IU MAURER SCHOOL OF LAW
GEO:39.165074;-86.526424
SUMMARY:New York Program Info Session
DESCRIPTION:New York Program Info Session  Are you interested in spending
  your summer in New York? CSO is hosting an info session for you to learn
  about IU Maurer's alumni-run program.  For those interested in exploring
  careers in New York and in the public sector. IU Alumnus and Adjunct Pro
 fessor Terrance Stroud has developed relationships with a number of publi
 c sector employers\, including the New York City Bar\, the New York Depar
 tment of Education\, and Brooklyn College's General Counsel's Office\, an
 d assists students with these opportunities or other public sector opport
 unities. Professor Stroud also organizes weekly networking events where p
 articipants can connect with and learn from alumni and other practitioner
 s working in a variety of settings in New York City\, including the judic
 iary\, the United Nations\, federal agencies\, politics\, academia\, non-
 profits\, and a DA's Office. These positions are unpaid\, but public inte
 rest positions will qualify the participant to apply for PILF and other s
 ummer public interest funding through Maurer. Students who obtain positio
 ns in New York through other means are also welcome to join the program f
 or its networking and educational benefits.  Learn more about the New Yor
 k Program and Professor Stroud here: https://www.legalevolution.org/tag/t
 errance-stroud/ (https://www.legalevolution.org/tag/terrance-stroud/)  RS
 VP by October 11th to attend.&#160\;
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  New York Program Info Session<br />  Ar
 e you interested in spending your summer in New York? CSO is hosting an i
 nfo session for you to learn about IU Maurer's alumni-run program.<br /><
 br />  For those interested in exploring careers in New York and in the p
 ublic sector. IU Alumnus and Adjunct Professor Terrance Stroud has develo
 ped relationships with a number of public sector employers\, including th
 e New York City Bar\, the New York Department of Education\, and Brooklyn
  College's General Counsel's Office\, and assists students with these opp
 ortunities or other public sector opportunities. Professor Stroud also or
 ganizes weekly networking events where participants can connect with and 
 learn from alumni and other practitioners working in a variety of setting
 s in New York City\, including the judiciary\, the United Nations\, feder
 al agencies\, politics\, academia\, non-profits\, and a DA's Office. Thes
 e positions are unpaid\, but public interest positions will qualify the p
 articipant to apply for PILF and other summer public interest funding thr
 ough Maurer. Students who obtain positions in New York through other mean
 s are also welcome to join the program for its networking and educational
  benefits.</p><p>  Learn more about the New York Program and Professor St
 roud here: <a href="https://www.legalevolution.org/tag/terrance-stroud/">
 https://www.legalevolution.org/tag/terrance-stroud/</a></p><p>  RSVP by O
 ctober 11th to attend.&#160\;</p>
UID:20261019T160000Z-2420145@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260916T182324Z
