BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Maurer School of Law
DTSTART:20261029T160000Z
DTEND:20261029T170000Z
LOCATION:Lowell E. Baier Hall - DeLaney Moot Court Room - 123
GEO:39.165074;-86.526424
SUMMARY:No License to Harm: Conversion Therapy and LGBTQ+ Health Law afte
 r Chiles
DESCRIPTION:In Chiles v. Salazar (2026)\, the Supreme Court held 8–1 th
 at Colorado's conversion therapy ban constitutes viewpoint discrimination
  subject to strict scrutiny.  Join Maurer's LGBTQ+ Project for a conversa
 tion with Prof. Heather McCabe (Saint Louis University) and Prof. Yvette 
 Butler (IU Maurer School of Law (https://law.indiana.edu/about/people/det
 ails?name=butler-yvette)) to explore the regulatory space Chiles preserve
 s and practical paths forward—including how legislatures can draft towa
 rd the Kagan concurrence\, and how Chiles's own logic may subject to stri
 ct scrutiny state laws that endorse gender-denying care while condemning 
 gender-affirming care.  RSVP by 9pm on October 26.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  In Chiles v. Salazar (2026)\, the Supre
 me Court held 8–1 that Colorado's conversion therapy ban constitutes vi
 ewpoint discrimination subject to strict scrutiny.<br />  Join Maurer's L
 GBTQ+ Project for a conversation with Prof. Heather McCabe (Saint Louis U
 niversity) and Prof. Yvette Butler (<a href="https://law.indiana.edu/abou
 t/people/details?name=butler-yvette">IU Maurer School of Law</a>) to expl
 ore the regulatory space Chiles preserves and practical paths forward—i
 ncluding how legislatures can draft toward the Kagan concurrence\, and ho
 w Chiles's own logic may subject to strict scrutiny state laws that endor
 se gender-denying care while condemning gender-affirming care.</p><p>  RS
 VP by 9pm on October 26.</p>
UID:20261029T160000Z-2435733@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260930T143059Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lawiub/event/2435733-no-license-to-harm-convers
 ion-therapy-and-lgbtq
CATEGORIES:Student-run
LAST-MODIFIED:20261001T130521Z
